This is Everly Sound Advisors' response to Item 6 of the staff's deficiency=
 letter, and the signed letter follows by mail.<br />
<br />
Everly Sound accepts Item 6. The staff is correct that between March 2015 a=
nd January 2017 the firm's electronic communications archive captured firm =
email but did not capture the two instant messaging platforms on which port=
folio managers discussed trade ideas with brokers, and that the firm theref=
ore did not make and keep the originals of all written communications recei=
ved and copies of all written communications sent relating to recommendatio=
ns made or proposed to be made, as Rule 204-2(a)(7) requires.<br />
<br />
The corrective action is as follows. Both platforms were connected to the f=
irm's archive on May 30, 2017 with full capture and seven-year retention. V=
endor-side history has been recovered for the period from June 2016 forward=
 and loaded into the archive; for the period before that the firm can recov=
er nothing and says so plainly rather than suggesting otherwise. Use of any=
 communications channel not connected to the archive is now prohibited by w=
ritten policy, and the policy names the permitted channels rather than desc=
ribing them generically, so that adding a channel requires an affirmative a=
mendment.<br />
<br />
Testing will be quarterly. I will personally certify to the managing member=
 each quarter that the channels in use match the channels named in the poli=
cy, and I will retain the certifications.<br />
<br />
I would rather over-explain the gap than have the staff find in a later exa=
mination that we described it narrowly. If the staff wants the vendor's rec=
overy report, I will send it.<br />
